course: dictionary
lesson: 14016
title: Making things magnetic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Magnetisation is the word for making something into a magnet. Stroke a steel nail with a magnet, always in the same direction, and the nail starts to pull pins towards it. That change is magnetisation. The ending -tion often means the process of doing something, like «action» or «station».
explain: The word can also mean how strongly something is magnetised. «The magnetisation of the iron bar was strong enough to lift a spoon.» Here the clues are strong and lift, so the word tells you about the bar's magnetic strength.
explain: Magnetisation can be lost. «Dropping the magnet on a hard floor caused a loss of magnetisation.» Heating a magnet or hitting it hard can destroy its magnetisation, so it stops working as a magnet. Words like loss and destroy tell you that the word means the magnetic state, not the process.
fact: Magnetisation means the process of making something into a magnet.
fact: Magnetisation can also mean how strongly something is magnetised.
fact: Stroking an iron nail with a magnet, always in one direction, can magnetise it.
fact: Heating or hitting a magnet can destroy its magnetisation.
fact: In American English the word is spelled «magnetization».
exercise: «Stroking the nail with a magnet in one direction is how its magnetisation begins.» What does magnetisation mean here? | *The process of making something into a magnet | The colour of the nail | Breaking something into small pieces | A heavy metal bar
exercise: Which action can destroy a magnet's magnetisation? | Shaking a box of paperclips | *Heating the magnet | Keeping the magnet in a dry drawer | Painting the magnet red
exercise: «Dropping the magnet caused a loss of magnetisation.» What has the magnet lost? | *Its magnetic power | Its colour | Its shape | Its weight
test: Dan rubbed a needle with a magnet until it could pick up pins. What is this process called? | *Magnetisation | Erosion | Condensation | Ignition
test: «The magnet lost its magnetisation after being hit with a hammer.» What does magnetisation mean here? | *Its magnetic strength | Its shine | Its size | Its temperature
exam: The American spelling of magnetisation is which word? | magnetism | *magnetization | magnetisashun | magnetisize
